        "description": "Reads and keeps nothing. Everything it works from is in the request and everything it makes is in the answer. From your setup steps (setup_steps: record:setup-steps rows, or the Get started answer you send as setup), your must-do list (must_do: record:waiting-on-you rows, or the whole waiting answer as things) and your hold setting (state), it answers cover { covered, key }: true while any required step is not done (the page draws only setup until then), null when nothing says, and key, the name your gate row gives the cover (required-setup when it gives none, so a missing key never leaves everything open). Beside it, hold: the one row that unblocks the most by your rank rules, every row that may hold in that order, how many times it can still be set aside today, the ways to hand it back and the stakes for turning the hold off. While the cover stands nothing else is held. Also answers what to keep: jobs (ai-job records for the AI-doable work it removed from the hold, each under a stable id so the same trigger is one job), held_fact ({ key, title } or null, the held thing to keep) and device_runs (the declared device tools to start when the held thing changed from kept_held, the one you last kept).",
